                "transcript": [
                  { "id": "ln-1", "ts": "0:00", "text": "Welcome back. In this unit we look at the product development lifecycle through the lens of AI-augmented workflows." },
                  { "id": "ln-2", "ts": "0:18", "text": "Understanding this lifecycle is critical — it's the backbone of everything a product manager does, from discovery to launch." },
                  { "id": "ln-3", "ts": "0:38", "text": "The lifecycle begins long before any code is written — with deep understanding of customer needs and unmet pain points.", "hasNote": true },
                  { "id": "ln-4", "ts": "0:58", "text": "Traditionally, this research phase was time-consuming — hours of interviews, synthesis workshops, affinity mapping." },
                  { "id": "ln-5", "ts": "1:14", "text": "This is exactly where AI tools can dramatically compress the research phase — turning 50 interviews into structured themes in minutes.", "hasNote": true },
                  { "id": "ln-6", "ts": "1:34", "text": "As we move into the ideation phase, AI can assist in generating innovative concepts based on the identified themes, fostering creativity and efficiency." },
                  { "id": "ln-7", "ts": "2:00", "text": "An MVP is not a smaller product. It's the smallest experiment you can run to test the riskiest assumption." }
                ]
